<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">The RAG-native trio (Embeddings v3 + Reranker v3 + Reader) covers the canonical 2026 RAG pipeline. The v2-base-* open-source variants are the on-prem path for teams that need to embed sensitive data on their own infrastructure; the four variants cover English, German, Chinese, and Code respectively and are all released under Apache 2.0 with commercial use explicitly granted. CLIP-v1 is the multimodal endpoint for teams that need to retrieve across text and image (e.g., an e-commerce product search that supports both "red sneakers" and an uploaded product photo).</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Jina API pricing: per-million-token billing in practice</h2>

<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Jina uses a flat per-million-token billing model across all nine endpoints, with a permanent free tier of 10,000 tokens/month (1M tokens/month for the Reader API) and a 50% discount on batch jobs. There are no credit packs, no subscriptions, no seat-based pricing — the model is "pay only for what you embed" and it scales linearly with usage.</p>

